go 1.25.0

// Dev-only workspace. Per go-bff-layout, shared-go resolves from the sibling
// ../../shared-go checkout so edits there are picked up live without a
// commit/push/version-bump cycle. CI and production build with GOWORK=off and
// resolve the version pinned in go.mod instead, so a change that only builds
// with this workspace active is a broken build — the dev loop's pinned_build
// gate exists to catch exactly that.
//
// This matters more here than in most repos: foto is the first service to mount
// a shared-go `tables` entity, and the patrulje lookup it needs
// (querier.GetByNumber) does not exist upstream yet. The moment somebody adds it
// in ../../shared-go everything compiles here and nothing compiles in CI, until
// shared-go is pushed and the pin bumped.
//
// cqrs and stream are deliberately NOT in the workspace: they resolve from the
// module proxy at the pinned version in every environment.
use (
	.
	../../shared-go
)
